WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 1.1 · Strategic Foundations
Purpose, vision and mission

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Three statements, three questions: why it should exist, the future you want, the work you will do.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.541
Three short statements that answer three different questions. Purpose: why should this exist? Vision: what future are we working towards? Mission: what will we do, for whom and how?

4
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:26.541
Three statements, in order

5
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:38.611
Purpose: Why it needs to exist: a specific unmet need, not your favourite solution. For example: So that young people who left school early can build skills and a working life.

6
00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:52.533
Vision: The future you want to help create, not your services or how big you will grow. For example: A neighbourhood where every young person has a way into good work, and good food is affordable.

7
00:00:52.533 --> 00:01:07.285
Mission: What you will do, for whom and how: “We help [people] achieve [change] through [approach].” For example: We bake and sell good bread, and train young people through paid traineeships, starting with one stall.

8
00:01:07.685 --> 00:01:08.285
Why they matter

9
00:01:08.285 --> 00:01:13.219
1. Purpose stays steady even if your first idea changes.

10
00:01:13.219 --> 00:01:19.263
2. Others join, fund or buy only if the reason matters beyond you.

11
00:01:19.263 --> 00:01:25.567
3. A clear mission tells you which opportunities to turn down.

12
00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:26.567
What they guide

13
00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:31.500
1. Your strategic objectives, which turn the mission into priorities.

14
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.433
2. Your Theory of Change, which starts from your vision.

15
00:01:36.433 --> 00:01:43.107
3. Your profile, website and registration form, which reuse the same words.

16
00:01:43.507 --> 00:01:44.107
What to avoid

17
00:01:44.107 --> 00:01:50.152
Starting from a solution (“we need an app”) instead of a need.

18
00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:55.085
A vision that lists services, revenue or growth targets.

19
00:01:55.085 --> 00:02:00.648
Publishing before testing the words with someone affected.

20
00:02:01.248 --> 00:02:03.048
You write your purpose, vision and mission, in that order.

21
00:02:03.048 --> 00:02:07.048
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:08.548 --> 00:02:11.648
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
